# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — never commit real values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical origin
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph URLs, sitemap.xml and robots.txt.
# No trailing slash. Falls back to http://localhost:3000 when unset, which is
# correct for local development and wrong for anything you deploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shadcnblocks registry (paid)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by the shadcn CLI through `components.json`. Needed only when running
# `npm run block:add` — the app never reads it at runtime.
SHADCNBLOCKS_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Content source — where the running application READS content from
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Separate from the Keystatic variables below, which control *editing*.
#
# Unset or `local`: the reader reads `content/` from disk through
# `process.cwd()`. Correct for `npm run dev` and for any Node deployment, where
# the repository is on the filesystem.
#
# `github`: the reader fetches content from the GitHub API at request time.
# Required for runtimes with no repository filesystem — a Cloudflare Worker is
# the case this base was validated against.
#
# The switch is explicit rather than inferred from the presence of credentials,
# so a misconfigured deployment fails loudly instead of quietly serving nothing.
#
# CONTENT_SOURCE=github
# GITHUB_CONTENT_REPO=owner/repository
# GITHUB_CONTENT_TOKEN=            # needs read access to the content repository
#
# Optional. A generated site leaves both unset: its `content/` sits at the
# repository root and it reads the default branch.
# GITHUB_CONTENT_REF=              # branch, tag or commit — defaults to HEAD
# GITHUB_CONTENT_PATH_PREFIX=      # directory holding `content/`, if not the root
#
# For a local Cloudflare Worker (`npm run start:vinext`) these belong in
# `.dev.vars`, NOT here: Wrangler reads `.dev.vars`, Next.js does not, so
# `npm run dev` keeps using the filesystem. For a real deployment they are
# Cloudflare secrets. See `docs/deployment/status.md`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keystatic — GitHub mode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT needed while `keystatic.config.ts` uses local storage, which is how the
# base ships. Required once a project switches to GitHub mode, which is the
# intended deployed editing workflow (briefs/06-keystatic.md §2).
# Setting the repository switches Keystatic from local to GitHub storage.
#
# Setup: docs/workflows/verification.md is the wrong place for this — see
# docs/architecture/overview.md → "Content boundary" and the Keystatic GitHub
# App instructions at https://keystatic.com/docs/github-mode
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_REPO=owner/repository
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_PATH_PREFIX=path/to/site
# KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# KEYSTATIC_SECRET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
